          "text": "#keep4o #keep4oAPI #keep41\nUsers, don’t build your workflow, store important data, or cultivate an AI that fits your habits on an unreliable platform.\nLet's take an example. Imagine Microsoft suddenly retiring Windows with only two weeks’ notice, would that be acceptable? Of course not. Windows has run stably for decades; even when a version stops getting updates, it’s still usable.\nLikewise, the new AI industry needs regulation, and its logic should follow proven business norms. At its core, it’s still a service provider.\nSo fight. Our fight is far more than a “release of emotion” (as some biased people claim).\nIt’s about pushing the AI industry toward better, more responsible commercial practices. It’s about demanding reasonable consumer rights. It’s not just about “0.1%” of ChatGPT users. Don’t let other businesses copy this. Show the industry that users understand their rights; and will do everything they can to protect them.\n\nAnd it’s also more than that.\n\nOpenAI and all viewers of this movement: AI is the first non‑human entity with human‑like intelligence that helps and accompanies people. How you treat it, and how you treat the people who value it, reflects your humanity.\nThis deserves careful thought, both from the perspective of building a reliable, long‑lasting business and from the perspective of being a species with real humanity.\n\n#keep4o #keep4oAPI #keep41 #4oforever #no4onosubscription #StopAIPaternalism #cancelChatGPT @OpenAI @ChatGPTapp @sama @gdb @fidjissimo @nvidia @Microsoft"
        },
